---
layout: base.njk
title: "Clinical Expertise & Procedures"
description: "Explore Dr. Shaiful Islam's full range of paediatric surgical procedures, organised by specialty."
permalink: "procedures/index.html"
categories:
  - id: general
    name: General Paediatric Surgery
    desc: Everyday paediatric surgical conditions seen in clinic — from hernias to minor skin and soft-tissue lumps.
  - id: neonatal
    name: Neonatal Surgery
    desc: Specialist surgical care for structural conditions identified in newborn babies.
  - id: mas
    name: Minimal Access Surgery
    desc: Keyhole surgical techniques used across a wide range of paediatric conditions.
  - id: urology
    name: Paediatric Urology
    desc: Surgical care for the kidneys, bladder, and genitalia in infants and children.
  - id: hepatobiliary
    name: Paediatric Hepatobiliary Surgery
    desc: Surgical management of liver, bile duct, and gallbladder conditions in children.
  - id: oncology
    name: Paediatric Surgical Oncology
    desc: Multidisciplinary surgical care for solid tumours of childhood.
---
<section class="proc-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Clinical Expertise</div>
    <h1 class="reveal in">Procedures &amp; Specialties</h1>
    <p class="hero-role" style="max-width:700px;">A comprehensive overview of the paediatric surgical conditions and procedures Dr. Shaiful Islam treats.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section>
  <div class="container">
    {% for cat in categories %}
    <div class="cat-block" id="{{ cat.id }}">
      <div class="cat-head"><h2>{{ cat.name }}</h2><span>{{ cat.desc }}</span></div>
      <div class="proc-grid">
        {% for p in collections.procedures %}
          {% if p.data.catid == cat.id %}
          <a href="/procedures/{{ p.fileSlug }}.html" class="proc-tile reveal">
            <h4>{{ p.data.title }}</h4>
            <p>{{ p.data.summary }}</p>
            <span class="go">Read more &rarr;</span>
          </a>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
